<title>UK: Imperial Tobacco makes strong debut.</title>
<headline>Imperial Tobacco makes strong debut.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Imperial Tobacco, one of four firms created from the demerger of Hanson, made a strong debut on the stock market, exceeding analysts' most optimistic expectations.</p>
<p>Imperial ended a heavy day of trading at 392-1/2p after opening at 390p. Hanson however fell 1-1/4p to 94p.</p>
<p>Analysts estimated the shares would start between 370p and 380p.</p>
<p>The shares were the most heavily traded in London, with more than 14 million trading hands.</p>
<p>Imperial's strong debut lifted shares in the tobacco and insurance group B.A.T Industries, which ended up 6p to 431-1/2p.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4027</p>
</text>
